  "question": {
    "text": "Which of the following statements is (are) incorrect?<br />\r<br />\r(i) Percentage ionic character in <math><mi>C</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>C</mi><mi>l</mi></math> bond is <math><mo>~</mo><mn>55</mn><mi>%</mi></math> . (Electronegativity values of <math><mi>C</mi><mi>s</mi></math> and <math><mi>C</mi><mi>l</mi></math> are <math><mn>0.7</mn></math> and <math><mn>3.0</mn></math> respectively)<br />\r<br />\r(ii) From <math><msub><mrow><mi>H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mi>O</mi></math> to <math><msub><mrow><mi>H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow><mi>O</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> , the geometry around <math><mi>O</mi></math> atom changes drastically.<br />\r<br />\r(iii) The most stable oxidation state for element with atomic number <math><mn>113</mn></math> is expected to be <math><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo></math><br />\r<br />\r(iv) The <math><msup><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></math> ionization energy of <math><mi>C</mi><mi>a</mi></math> is greater than <math><msup><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></math> ionization energy of it but lower than <math><msup><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></math> ionization energy of K.",
